    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Ocean Colour Scene’s third album, Marchin’ Already, is a bright, hook-heavy Britpop record that broadens the band’s sound with blues-rock grit, soulful backing vocals, and a stronger rhythmic pull than its predecessors. Released in 1997 on MCA in the U.S., it features the UK chart-topping single “Hundred Mile High City” and other standout tracks such as “Better Day,” “Traveller’s Tune,” and “It’s a Beautiful Thing,” which helped define the group’s most commercially successful period.\n\nThe album arrived at the height of the Britpop era and was widely seen as confirmation that Ocean Colour Scene had moved from promising contenders to major players. Its blend of muscular guitars, retro soul touches, and melodic choruses gave it broad appeal, and its success was reinforced by strong chart performance and enduring fan favorites that have kept it central to the band’s catalog.",
